<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">League of the Public Weal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1465">1465</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The League of the Public Weal was an alliance of great French nobles formed in 1465 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a>, led by Charles of Charolais (later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a>), Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany, Duke John II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> and the king's brother Charles of Berry. After the indecisive Battle of Montlhéry, Louis made large concessions in the treaties of Conflans and Saint-Maur, which he soon undermined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-the-public-weal.jpg" alt="League of the Public Weal" width="320" height="494" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Étienne Colaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerre_du_Bien_public.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Francis II, who had no son, joined the <b>League of the Public Weal</b> against Louis XI in 1465 and later sheltered princes in revolt against the regency of Anne of Beaujeu, giving the crown reason to intervene.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Duchy of Brittany · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
